A computed goto that gives a VLA's storage back, which only the IR backend
does. The legacy backend reclaims nothing before the function returns - the
same design that keeps it out of vla_in_loop and vla_scope_exit - so this is
skipped there rather than muted: there is no bug here waiting to be fixed and
flagged.

gcc reclaims nothing on a computed goto either, so unlike its two neighbours
this fixture is not a gcc-parity test. See its header.
